<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alejandro O'Reilly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1723–1794</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Alexander O'Reilly</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alejandro O'Reilly was an Irish-born general in Spanish service. In 1769 he arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> with troops, put down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">creole</a> Rebellion of 1768 against Spanish rule, executed its leaders and established Spanish law and administration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> before leaving in 1770. He later reformed the Spanish army and led a failed attack on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> in 1775.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alejandro-oreilly.jpg" alt="Alejandro O'Reilly" width="320" height="472" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco Goya · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alejandro_O%27Reilly_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
